{"title":"Substation Engineer Roadmap","role":"Substation Engineer","summary":"A Substation Engineer works on the design, construction, testing, commissioning, operation, maintenance and protection of electrical substations. The pathway combines power systems, high-voltage engineering, protection, switchgear, transformers, SCADA and electrical safety.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Substation Engineer is a directly aligned career for Electrical & Electronics Engineering (EEE)."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build electrical fundamentals, power systems, protection, switchgear, safety and substation project experience."},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in substation design, protection & control, commissioning, testing or SCADA/automation."},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Move toward senior engineering, project ownership, protection coordination and substation system design."},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Develop expertise in digital substations, renewable-grid integration, automation, grid resilience and advanced protection."}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Substation Engineer works on the design, construction, testing, commissioning, operation, maintenance and protection of electrical substations. The pathway combines power systems, high-voltage engineering, protection, switchgear, transformers, SCADA and electrical safety."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"tex